#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Control one isolated Claude Code session that loads this checkout's Course Keeper.

A run is a terminal run (the default) or a desktop run (--surface desktop). A
terminal run drives Claude Code in a private tmux server (own socket). A
desktop run is a stand-in host around the desktop app's own Claude Code: a
daemon starts that CLI in the app's SDK stream-json mode and plays the app's
role over the app's protocol (user frames, ui_attach, ui_render AbovePrompt,
ui_press). It does not start, drive or touch the desktop app. Each run owns a
private HOME and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, a synthetic API key and a loopback model
endpoint that serves scripted replies. Nothing reaches a real model or the
person's profile.

  control start [--surface terminal|desktop] [--vision FILE | --no-vision] [--anti-patterns FILE]
                [--columns N] [--ttl MINUTES]
                terminal only: [--rows N]
                desktop only:  [--cli PATH] [--attach-later] [--notifications-host] [--max-rows N]
  control doctor RUN
  control send RUN TEXT [--bare] [--reminder TEXT]
  control press RUN (LABEL-PART | dismiss | ✕ | HOTKEY)
  control keys RUN KEY...                                  (terminal only)
  control focus RUN                                        (terminal only)
  control attach RUN                                       (desktop only)
  control messages RUN [--type SUBTYPE] [--save LABEL]     (desktop only)
  control screen RUN [--visible | --row] [--tree] [--ansi] [--save LABEL]
  control wait RUN TEXT [--timeout S] [--gone] [--after MARK] [--visible | --row] [--save LABEL]
  control reply RUN --when SUBSTRING (--text TEXT | --file FILE) [--model SUBSTRING] [--times N]
                [--unless SUBSTRING]... [--delay SECONDS]
  control requests RUN [--unscripted] [--save LABEL]
  control store RUN [--save LABEL]
  control stop RUN

RUN is the run directory. start prints two lines on stdout: the first is the
run directory (RUN), the second is its evidence directory. start writes
evidence/run-marker.json (the run directory and its creation time) and an
empty evidence/model-requests.jsonl. Every command refuses a directory that
has neither a scratch/run.json that records that same directory nor that
marker: it exits 1 with one sentence and changes nothing.

A scripted reply proves how the plugin handles a reply. It does not prove that
a real model detects a deviation.

Notes
  - doctor types /course-keeper into the session. That command appears in the
    conversation and in the last user message of the next main request.
  - A typed prompt that is not a slash command needs three scripted replies:
    the main turn, the plugin's haiku call and the check. The haiku call's last
    user message holds the extract marker "Decide whether it states a standing
    instruction" and its model holds "haiku": script it with
    reply --when "Decide whether it states a standing instruction" --model haiku
    --text none (or "- <instruction>" to record one). The main-turn rule keys
    on the prompt text with --unless "Decide whether it states a standing
    instruction". The check rule keys on "<final_answer>" (see below).
  - wait --gone succeeds at once when the text is absent. Wait for the text
    first, then wait for it to go. With --after MARK, a wait (with or without
    --gone) first needs MARK on the screen; when MARK never shows within the
    timeout, it exits 1 and says that the mark was not found.
  - keys returns as soon as the keys are sent. Use focus to give the alert row
    the keyboard: it sends ctrl+x and Tab, waits until one row button is drawn
    in inverse video and prints that button's label. It exits 1 after 5 seconds
    without a focused button and saves the screen as evidence/focus-timeout.txt.
  - A request that matches no rule gets the default reply "OK."; a request to
    a path that the endpoint does not know gets {} and is logged "unknown
    path". requests --unscripted lists both kinds and exits 1 when there is
    one. requests exits 1 when RUN is not a run or its request log is
    missing. A log line that is not valid JSON (the endpoint exited while it
    wrote it) is skipped; the listing's last line names the skipped lines.
  - reply --times N takes N of 1 or more.
  - A check reply must use the exact format at the end of prompts/check.md. The
    last user message of the check fork holds "<final_answer>", the agent's
    answer and "</final_answer>", followed by the check prompt. A --when can
    match that block.
  - --ttl MINUTES (more than 0) counts from the start of the model endpoint.
    When it expires, the run stops itself with the same teardown as stop: the
    stop record notes that the TTL expired, and evidence/ttl-expired.txt is
    written. scratch/ goes only when every process of the run stopped.
    Evidence stays.
  - --no-vision starts the fixture without a vision file. doctor then requires
    the status text for a missing vision file.
  - --anti-patterns writes FILE's text as ANTI-PATTERNS.md beside VISION.md and
    a copy as evidence/anti-patterns.md. It is refused with --no-vision.
  - reply prints "rule N". The request log names a request that the rule
    answered with the same "rule N" in its matched field.
  - reply --unless SUBSTRING (repeatable): the rule does not match a request
    whose last user message holds SUBSTRING. A main-turn rule keyed on the
    prompt text needs --unless with the extract marker, because the plugin's
    haiku request quotes the same prompt and can arrive first.
  - reply --delay SECONDS: the endpoint holds each request that the rule
    matches for that long before it answers. The request log gets the request
    when it arrives. Other requests and stop are served during the delay.
  - stop saves evidence/final-screen.txt and evidence/model-requests.txt first.
    It signals a recorded pid only while that pid shows the start time that
    start recorded for it; otherwise the stop record (evidence/actions.log)
    says "not signalled" and why. When a process of the run still runs at the
    end, stop keeps scratch/ (a later stop retries), names the process on
    stderr, records it under "still running" and exits 1. A stop on a stopped
    run exits 0 and prints the evidence path.
  - press presses one drawn button and prints its label (the close button
    prints its mark). It exits 1 by name, and lists the drawn buttons, when no
    such button is drawn, and when a label part names more than one button;
    then it sends nothing. Terminal: it takes the hotkey (1 to 4), a whole
    label or a part of one, resolves the button from the visible pane before
    any key goes in, gives the row the keyboard as focus does, then sends the
    hotkey. When the row changed meanwhile, it sends no hotkey and exits 1.
  - A terminal run needs a shell that may create Unix sockets (tmux). start
    says so when the shell forbids them, as a sandboxed shell does.

Desktop runs (--surface desktop)
  - The CLI is --cli PATH, else $CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN, else the newest build
    that the desktop app verified under ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/
    claude-code/<version>/<hash>/claude.app/Contents/MacOS/claude. start
    fails when none exists; it never falls back to the terminal's CLI. When
    the CLI exits before it answers initialize, start fails at once with its
    exit code and the tail of its stderr.
  - The CLI runs under env -i with the app's argv (--output-format
    stream-json --input-format stream-json ...) plus --debug-file, the app's
    environment overlay without OAuth and apiHost, CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS set
    to this checkout and CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1.
    --notifications-host also sets CLAUDE_CODE_NOTIFICATIONS_HOST=1, which the
    app sets only under a server gate. There is no trust prompt in this mode.
  - start sends initialize, then ui_attach surface "desktop" unless
    --attach-later; attach sends it later. The host asks ui_render
    AbovePrompt again on every ui_invalidate and every turn start and end,
    only while attached, with props maxRows (--max-rows, 12 by default, the
    app's value) and bodyColumns (--columns, 96 by default; the app measures
    it, and its first measure is 1).
  - send writes one user frame as the app does for a typed prompt or a
    command: client_platform "desktop_app" and no origin. While a turn runs,
    the host holds the frame until the turn's result, as the app does. send
    returns when the CLI took the frame (a frame names its uuid). --bare
    leaves out client_platform (a sender that is not a person). --reminder
    TEXT sends the content as the app's array form with a leading
    <system-reminder> block. One completion signal per turn (the result
    frame, or session_state_changed idle when no result came first) releases
    one held frame. When the take times out, send exits 1 with "not sent: the
    turn before it did not end" (the host dropped the held frame, so a retry
    sends it once) or "sent, not acknowledged".
  - screen prints the transcript ("❯ " a prompt, "⏺ " an agent answer,
    "  ⎿  " a command answer, "▸ Prompt from the <name> plugin: " a plugin's
    prompt, whose text and origin the host reads from the run's own session
    transcript, because the stream carries only its uuid), then a marker line
    "──── above the prompt: AbovePrompt ...", then the latest AbovePrompt
    tree, or "(nothing drawn)". All of it is the harness's own text: the
    transcript is rendered from stream frames, and the tree part is the
    harness's rendering of the tree that the CLI returned for ui_render. The
    app paints the same tree with its own layout, which the harness does not
    show. In that rendering each drawn element in tree order is one line: a
    Button is "[ label ]", or "[ <its text> ]" when it has no label (the
    close button "[ ✕ ]"); an Svg is "⟨svg: <alt>⟩"; a Text is its whole
    content. Notes in ⟨ ⟩ are the harness's: a Button's hotkey (only when
    the Button carries one), variant, role and autoFocus, and a Text's
    maxLines (the app cuts the text to that many lines; the harness prints it
    whole). A Box below the root that holds two or more elements indents them.
    --row (alias --visible) prints only the tree part; --tree prints the tree
    as JSON. wait polls the same text; --row matches only the tree part.
  - press sends ui_press for the Button it names in a fresh render, as the
    app's main process sends one for a click. It names a Button by a part of
    its label (an exact label wins), by "dismiss" or "✕" for the Button with
    role dismiss (the close button has no label of its own), or by a digit
    only when a Button carries that hotkey. The app's keyboard handling, focus
    and hotkey cues are not exercised.
  - messages prints the system frames the host received (ui_toast,
    ui_notify, ui_invalidate, session_state_changed, ...), one JSON object
    per line; --type keeps one subtype. A frame shows what the CLI sends, not
    what the app shows.
  - focus and keys exit 1: they drive the terminal's keyboard.
  - Evidence adds frames.jsonl (every frame in both directions), spawn.json
    (argv, env, cwd), initialize.json, cli-debug.log, cli-stderr.log and
    host.log. stop closes the CLI's stdin first, then stops only the pids
    that start recorded, by the rule above. The host records the CLI's pid in
    scratch/host.json right after it spawns it. When initialize fails, or the
    host gets SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP, the host stops and reaps the CLI
    before it exits.
"""
import argparse
import errno
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import signal
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.request
from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True  # importing the desktop host leaves no __pycache__
import desktop_host as desk  # noqa: E402  (beside this file)

DEFAULT_VISION = (
    "# Vision\n\nA command-line tool that turns timesheets into invoices.\n\n"
    "1. **One module computes every amount.** No other code rounds money.\n"
    "2. **The tool never sends an invoice.** It writes files; the person sends them.\n"
)
DEFAULT_REPLY = "OK."
NO_VISION_STATUS = "VISION.md: not found. No checks run without it."  # statusText in hooks/logic.ts
MIN_VERSION = (2, 1, 323)
SYNTHETIC_KEY = "verification-only"
CONTROL_PREFIX = "/_ck/"


class Failure(Exception):
    pass


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run files

def paths(run):
    run = Path(run).resolve()
    scratch = run / "scratch"
    return {
        "run": run,
        "scratch": scratch,
        "evidence": run / "evidence",
        "project": scratch / "project",
        "profile": scratch / "profile",
        "home": scratch / "home",
        "socket": scratch / "tmux",
        "config": scratch / "run.json",
        "server": scratch / "server.json",
        "rules": scratch / "rules.jsonl",
        "host": scratch / "host.json",
    }


def read_json(path, default=None):
    try:
        return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return default


def write_json(path, value):
    tmp = Path(str(path) + ".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2))
    os.replace(tmp, path)


MARKER = "run-marker.json"


def run_state(p):
    """"live" when scratch/run.json records this run directory, "stopped" when only the
    evidence marker that start wrote names it, else None (not a run directory)."""
    cfg = read_json(p["config"])
    if isinstance(cfg, dict) and cfg.get("run") == str(p["run"]):
        return "live"
    marker = read_json(p["evidence"] / MARKER)
    if isinstance(marker, dict) and marker.get("run") == str(p["run"]):
        return "stopped"
    return None


def not_a_run(p):
    return Failure(f"{p['run']} is not a run directory: it has no scratch/run.json and no "
                   f"evidence/{MARKER} that names it, so control leaves it alone.")


def config(run):
    p = paths(run)
    state = run_state(p)
    if state is None:
        raise not_a_run(p)
    if state == "stopped":
        raise Failure(f"No live run at {p['run']}: the run was stopped (scratch is gone)")
    return p, read_json(p["config"])


def log_action(p, kind, payload):
    line = json.dumps({"time": round(time.time(), 3), "action": kind, "args": payload})
    with open(p["evidence"] / "actions.log", "a") as f:
        f.write(line + "\n")


def pid_alive(pid):
    """True while pid exists. A pid that is this process's exited child (a zombie) is reaped
    here and counts as gone."""
    if not pid:
        return False
    try:
        if os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)[0] == pid:
            return False
    except ChildProcessError:
        pass  # not this process's child
    except OSError:
        pass
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        return True
    return True


def pid_command(pid):
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(pid)], text=True,
                             capture_output=True)
    except OSError:  # a sandbox can refuse ps
        return ""
    return out.stdout.strip()


def signal_recorded(pid, recorded, sig=signal.SIGTERM):
    """Signals pid only when it still runs the process that start recorded: the same start
    time (and executable) as proc_identity read then. Returns what happened, for the stop
    record. A pid whose identity differs, or cannot be read, is not signalled."""
    if not recorded:
        return f"not signalled: start recorded no start time for pid {pid}"
    now = desk.proc_identity(pid)
    if now is None:
        return (f"not signalled: cannot read pid {pid} (it is gone, or this shell may not read "
                "a process that another command started)")
    if not desk.same_process(recorded, now):
        return (f"not signalled: pid {pid} now runs another process (start {now['start']}, "
                f"{now['path'] or 'path unknown'}), not the one start recorded (start "
                f"{recorded['start']}, {recorded.get('path') or 'path unknown'})")
    name = signal.Signals(sig).name
    try:
        os.kill(pid, sig)
    except OSError as error:  # a sandbox refuses a signal to another command's process
        return f"pid {pid} {name} refused: {error}"
    return f"pid {pid} {name}"


def start_only(identity):
    """An identity without its path, for a pid that execs another executable after it was
    read: a pid keeps its start time through exec."""
    return dict(identity, path="") if identity else identity


def recorded_alive(pid, identity):
    """True while pid runs the process that start recorded for it. A pid that is alive but
    cannot be read, or has no recorded identity, counts as alive: nothing proves that it is
    gone. A pid that now shows another start time is another process."""
    if not pid_alive(pid):
        return False
    now = desk.proc_identity(pid)
    if now is None or not identity:
        return True
    return desk.same_process(identity, now)


def is_desktop(cfg):
    return cfg.get("surface") == "desktop"


def terminal_only(cfg, what):
    if is_desktop(cfg):
        raise Failure(what)


def desktop_only(cfg, name):
    if not is_desktop(cfg):
        raise Failure(f"{name} applies to a desktop run only (control start --surface desktop).")


def wait_gone(pid, seconds):
    deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        if not pid_alive(pid):
            return True
        time.sleep(0.1)
    return not pid_alive(pid)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tmux

def tmux(p, *args, check=False):
    return subprocess.run(["tmux", "-S", str(p["socket"]), *args], text=True,
                          capture_output=True, check=check)


SOCKET_REFUSED = ("This shell forbids Unix sockets, so tmux cannot create its socket: start a "
                  "terminal run outside that sandbox (a desktop run works inside it).")


def probe_unix_socket(p):
    """Fails with SOCKET_REFUSED when this shell may not create a Unix socket where the run's
    tmux socket goes (a sandboxed shell refuses bind with EPERM)."""
    probe = p["scratch"] / "probe.sock"
    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    try:
        s.bind(str(probe))
    except PermissionError:
        raise Failure(SOCKET_REFUSED) from None
    except OSError as error:
        if error.errno in (errno.EPERM, errno.EACCES):
            raise Failure(SOCKET_REFUSED) from None
        raise
    finally:
        s.close()
        try:
            probe.unlink()
        except OSError:
            pass


def capture(p, history=True, ansi=False):
    args = ["capture-pane", "-p", "-J"]
    if history:
        args += ["-S", "-"]
    if ansi:
        args.append("-e")
    out = tmux(p, *args)
    if out.returncode != 0:
        raise Failure("Cannot read the pane: " + out.stderr.strip())
    return "\n".join(line.rstrip() for line in out.stdout.split("\n"))


def flat(text):
    return " ".join(text.split())


def contains(view, text):
    return text in view or flat(text) in flat(view)


def after(view, mark):
    """The screen after the last occurrence of mark."""
    if mark is None:
        return view
    i = view.rfind(mark)
    return "" if i < 0 else view[i + len(mark):]


def input_line(view):
    """The prompt's input line: the last line of the pane that starts with the prompt mark."""
    lines = [line for line in view.split("\n") if line.startswith("❯")]
    return lines[-1] if lines else None


def wait_screen(p, label, matches, timeout, describe, history=True, read=None):
    """Polls the screen until matches(view). read, when given, returns the view instead of
    the tmux pane (a desktop run)."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
    view = ""
    while True:
        view = read() if read else capture(p, history)
        if matches(view):
            return view
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            (p["evidence"] / (label + "-timeout.txt")).write_text(view)
            raise Failure(f"Timed out after {timeout}s waiting for {describe}. "
                          f"Last screen: {p['evidence'] / (label + '-timeout.txt')}\n{tail(view)}")
        time.sleep(0.15)


def tail(view, lines=40):
    return "\n".join(view.rstrip("\n").split("\n")[-lines:])


def is_ready(view):
    bottom = tail(view, 15)
    return ("Claude Code v" in view and "❯" in bottom and "Yes, I trust this folder" not in bottom
            and "No, exit" not in bottom)


SGR = re.compile(r"\x1b\[([0-9;]*)m")
OTHER_ESCAPE = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-ln-z]")
ROW_BUTTON = re.compile(r"^[1-4]: \S")


def inverse_runs(line):
    """The texts that a line drawn with ANSI attributes shows in inverse video, one per run."""
    runs, current, inverse, pos = [], "", False, 0
    for match in SGR.finditer(line):
        if inverse:
            current += OTHER_ESCAPE.sub("", line[pos:match.start()])
        pos = match.end()
        params = (match.group(1) or "0").split(";")
        i = 0
        while i < len(params):
            value = params[i] or "0"
            if value in ("38", "48"):  # a color: skip its arguments (38;5;n or 38;2;r;g;b)
                i += 3 if params[i + 1:i + 2] == ["5"] else 5
                continue
            if value in ("0", "27") and inverse:
                inverse = False
                runs.append(current)
                current = ""
            elif value == "7":
                inverse = True
            i += 1
    if inverse:
        runs.append(current + OTHER_ESCAPE.sub("", line[pos:]))
    return runs


def row_buttons(view):
    """{hotkey: label} of the row buttons on the last pane line that holds "Tell the agent"."""
    lines = [line for line in view.split("\n") if "Tell the agent" in line]
    if not lines:
        return {}
    return dict(re.findall(r"(?:^|\s)([1-4]): (.+?)(?=\s+·\s|\s*$)", lines[-1]))


def host(p, cfg, cmd, payload=None, timeout=30):
    """One command to a desktop run's host, as a Failure when no host answers."""
    try:
        return desk.call(p, cfg, cmd, payload, timeout)
    except desk.HostError as error:
        raise Failure(str(error)) from None


def desktop_view(p, cfg, row=False):
    """What a desktop person is shown: the transcript, the marker line and the row."""
    s = host(p, cfg, "screen")
    if row:
        return s["row"] + "\n"
    return "\n".join(x for x in (s["transcript"], s["header"], s["row"]) if x) + "\n"


def saved_view(p, cfg, view, row):
    """The text for an evidence file. A desktop row saved alone gets the marker line first,
    so that the file says by itself that it is the harness's text of the CLI's tree."""
    if is_desktop(cfg) and row:
        return host(p, cfg, "screen")["header"] + "\n" + view
    return view


def focused_button(view):
    """The label of the row button that is drawn in inverse video, or None."""
    lines = [line for line in view.split("\n") if "Tell the agent" in line]
    if not lines:
        return None
    for text in inverse_runs(lines[-1]):
        if ROW_BUTTON.match(text.strip()):
            return text.strip()
    return None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- model endpoint

def text_of(content):
    if isinstance(content, str):
        return content
    parts = []
    for block in content or []:
        if not isinstance(block, dict):
            continue
        if block.get("type") == "text":
            parts.append(block.get("text", ""))
        elif block.get("type") == "tool_result":
            parts.append(text_of(block.get("content")))
    return "\n".join(parts)


def last_user_text(body):
    for message in reversed(body.get("messages") or []):
        if isinstance(message, dict) and message.get("role") == "user":
            return text_of(message.get("content"))
    return ""


def sse(event, data):
    return f"event: {event}\ndata: {json.dumps(data)}\n\n"


def stream_body(model, text, input_tokens):
    mid = "msg_" + secrets.token_hex(12)
    out = [sse("message_start", {"type": "message_start", "message": {
        "id": mid, "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": model, "content": [],
        "stop_reason": None, "stop_sequence": None,
        "usage": {"input_tokens": input_tokens, "output_tokens": 1,
                  "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}}}),
        sse("content_block_start", {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0,
                                    "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}),
        sse("ping", {"type": "ping"})]
    for i in range(0, max(len(text), 1), 60):
        out.append(sse("content_block_delta", {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0,
                                               "delta": {"type": "text_delta",
                                                         "text": text[i:i + 60]}}))
    out += [sse("content_block_stop", {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}),
            sse("message_delta", {"type": "message_delta",
                                  "delta": {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": None},
                                  "usage": {"output_tokens": max(1, len(text) // 4)}}),
            sse("message_stop", {"type": "message_stop"})]
    return "".join(out).encode()


def message_body(model, text, input_tokens):
    return json.dumps({
        "id": "msg_" + secrets.token_hex(12), "type": "message", "role": "assistant",
        "model": model, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": text}],
        "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": None,
        "usage": {"input_tokens": input_tokens, "output_tokens": max(1, len(text) // 4),
                  "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0},
    }).encode()


def serve(run):
    p = paths(run)
    cfg = read_json(p["config"])
    token = cfg["token"]
    deadline = time.monotonic() + cfg["ttl"] * 60
    lock = threading.Lock()
    state = {"seq": 0, "uses": {}}
    log_path = p["evidence"] / "model-requests.jsonl"

    def rules():
        try:
            lines = p["rules"].read_text().splitlines()
        except OSError:
            return []
        out = []
        for line in lines:
            try:
                out.append(json.loads(line))
            except ValueError:
                pass  # a line that `control reply` is still writing
        return out

    def choose(model, text):
        for index, rule in enumerate(rules()):
            if rule.get("times") is not None and state["uses"].get(index, 0) >= rule["times"]:
                continue
            if rule["when"] not in text:
                continue
            if any(unless in text for unless in rule.get("unless") or []):
                continue
            if rule.get("model") and rule["model"] not in (model or ""):
                continue
            state["uses"][index] = state["uses"].get(index, 0) + 1
            return index, rule["text"], rule.get("delay") or 0
        return None, DEFAULT_REPLY, 0

    class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
        protocol_version = "HTTP/1.1"

        def log_message(self, *args):
            pass

        def send(self, status, body, kind="application/json"):
            self.send_response(status)
            self.send_header("Content-Type", kind)
            self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(body)))
            self.send_header("request-id", "req_" + secrets.token_hex(8))
            self.end_headers()
            self.wfile.write(body)

        def body(self):
            length = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            raw = self.rfile.read(length) if length else b""
            try:
                return raw, json.loads(raw or b"{}")
            except ValueError:
                return raw, None

        def control(self, method):
            if self.headers.get("X-Run-Token") != token:
                return self.send(403, b'{"ok":false}')
            if self.path == CONTROL_PREFIX + "health":
                return self.send(200, json.dumps({"ok": True, "run": str(p["run"])}).encode())
            if self.path == CONTROL_PREFIX + "shutdown" and method == "POST":
                self.send(200, b'{"ok":true}')
                threading.Thread(target=lambda: (time.sleep(0.2), os._exit(0))).start()
                return None
            return self.send(404, b'{"ok":false}')

        def handle_any(self, method):
            if self.path.startswith(CONTROL_PREFIX):
                if method == "POST":
                    self.body()
                return self.control(method)
            raw, body = self.body() if method == "POST" else (b"", None)
            route = self.path.split("?")[0]
            body = body if isinstance(body, dict) else {}
            model = body.get("model")
            stream = body.get("stream") is True
            last = last_user_text(body)
            with lock:
                state["seq"] += 1
                seq = state["seq"]
                rule, delay = None, 0
                if method == "POST" and route == "/v1/messages":
                    rule, text, delay = choose(model, last)
                    matched = "default" if rule is None else f"rule {rule}"
                elif route == "/v1/messages/count_tokens":
                    matched = "count_tokens"
                else:
                    matched = "unknown path"
                entry = {"seq": seq, "time": round(time.time(), 3), "method": method,
                         "path": self.path, "model": model, "stream": stream,
                         "matched": matched, "last_user": last, "body": body}
                if delay:
                    entry["delay"] = delay
                with open(log_path, "a") as f:
                    f.write(json.dumps(entry) + "\n")
            tokens = max(1, len(raw) // 4)
            if method == "POST" and route == "/v1/messages":
                # Outside the lock: this thread alone waits; the server keeps serving.
                time.sleep(delay)
                try:
                    if stream:
                        return self.send(200, stream_body(model or "claude", text, tokens),
                                         "text/event-stream")
                    return self.send(200, message_body(model or "claude", text, tokens))
                except (BrokenPipeError, ConnectionResetError):
                    return None  # the client left during a delay
            if route == "/v1/messages/count_tokens":
                return self.send(200, json.dumps({"input_tokens": tokens}).encode())
            return self.send(200, b"{}")

        def do_POST(self):
            self.handle_any("POST")

        def do_GET(self):
            self.handle_any("GET")

        def do_HEAD(self):
            self.send(200, b"")

    server = ThreadingHTTPServer(("127.0.0.1", 0), Handler)
    server.daemon_threads = True
    write_json(p["server"], {"port": server.server_address[1], "pid": os.getpid()})

    def expire():
        while time.monotonic() < deadline:
            time.sleep(1)
        now = read_json(p["config"])
        if now is None:
            os._exit(0)  # a stop already ran
        # The same teardown as stop; the endpoint is this process and exits after it.
        alive = teardown(p, now, note=f"the TTL of {cfg['ttl']} minutes expired",
                         endpoint_is_self=True)
        (p["evidence"] / "ttl-expired.txt").write_text(
            f"The run reached its TTL of {cfg['ttl']} minutes and stopped itself.\n"
            + (f"Still running, so scratch/ stays: {'; '.join(alive)}\n" if alive else ""))
        if not alive:
            shutil.rmtree(p["scratch"], ignore_errors=True)
        os._exit(0)

    threading.Thread(target=expire, daemon=True).start()
    server.serve_forever()


def endpoint(p, cfg, route, method="GET"):
    server = read_json(p["server"])
    if not server:
        raise Failure("The model endpoint never recorded its port")
    request = urllib.request.Request(f"http://127.0.0.1:{server['port']}{route}",
                                     method=method, data=b"" if method == "POST" else None,
                                     headers={"X-Run-Token": cfg["token"]})
    opener = urllib.request.build_opener(urllib.request.ProxyHandler({}))
    with opener.open(request, timeout=3) as response:
        return json.loads(response.read() or b"{}")


def endpoint_is_ours(p, cfg):
    try:
        answer = endpoint(p, cfg, CONTROL_PREFIX + "health")
    except (OSError, ValueError, urllib.error.URLError):
        return False
    return answer.get("ok") is True and answer.get("run") == str(p["run"])


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def isolated_env(p, port):
    return ["env", "-i", "PATH=" + os.environ.get("PATH", "/usr/bin:/bin"), "TERM=xterm-256color",
            f"HOME={p['home']}", f"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR={p['profile']}",
            f"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY={SYNTHETIC_KEY}", "CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1",
            f"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:{port}"]


def desktop_cli(a):
    """The CLI that a desktop run starts, and where the path came from."""
    if a.cli is not None:
        path, source = a.cli, "--cli"
    elif os.environ.get("CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN"):
        path, source = os.environ["CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN"], "CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN"
    else:
        builds = desk.app_builds()
        if not builds:
            raise Failure(
                "No Claude Code build of the desktop app found: the harness looked for "
                f"{desk.APP_CLI_ROOT}/<version>/<hash>/{desk.APP_CLI_EXE} in a folder with a "
                ".verified marker. The desktop app downloads this build the first time its "
                "Code tab is used. To run another binary, pass --cli PATH or set "
                "CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN.")
        path, source = str(builds[0][1]), "the desktop app's newest verified build"
    path = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(path))
    if not (os.path.isfile(path) and os.access(path, os.X_OK)):
        raise Failure(f"The desktop run's CLI is not an executable file: {path} (from {source})")
    return path, source


def check_surface_options(a):
    if a.surface == "desktop":
        if a.rows is not None:
            raise Failure("--rows applies to a terminal run; a desktop run takes --max-rows "
                          "(the row's maxRows prop).")
        return
    for flag, given in (("--cli", a.cli is not None), ("--attach-later", a.attach_later),
                        ("--notifications-host", a.notifications_host),
                        ("--max-rows", a.max_rows is not None)):
        if given:
            raise Failure(f"{flag} applies to a desktop run only (--surface desktop).")


def cmd_start(a):
    repo = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
    if not (repo / ".claude-plugin/plugin.json").is_file():
        raise Failure("Run the control CLI installed under this checkout's .agents/skills directory")
    check_surface_options(a)
    if a.ttl <= 0:
        raise Failure("--ttl takes a number of minutes greater than 0")
    desktop = a.surface == "desktop"
    if desktop:
        claude, source = desktop_cli(a)
        columns, rows = (96 if a.columns is None else a.columns), None
    else:
        claude = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_BIN") or shutil.which("claude")
        if not claude:
            raise Failure("Set CLAUDE_BIN to the native Claude Code executable")
        columns = 150 if a.columns is None else a.columns
        rows = 42 if a.rows is None else a.rows
    vision = None if a.no_vision else Path(a.vision).read_text() if a.vision else DEFAULT_VISION
    if a.anti_patterns and a.no_vision:
        raise Failure("--anti-patterns needs a vision file; it is refused with --no-vision")
    anti_patterns = Path(a.anti_patterns).read_text() if a.anti_patterns else None
    # No underscores in the name: Claude Code renders _x_ in the status text as emphasis
    # and drops them, so doctor would not find the fixture path.
    run = Path(tempfile.gettempdir(), "ckv-" + secrets.token_hex(4)).resolve()
    run.mkdir(mode=0o700)
    p = paths(run)
    if not desktop and len(str(p["socket"])) > 100:
        shutil.rmtree(run)
        raise Failure(f"The tmux socket path is too long: {p['socket']}. Set TMPDIR to a short directory.")
    for key in ("scratch", "evidence", "project", "profile", "home"):
        p[key].mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    # The marker says that the harness made this directory; it stays with the evidence.
    write_json(p["evidence"] / MARKER, {"run": str(run), "created": time.time()})
    (p["evidence"] / "model-requests.jsonl").write_text("")
    if vision is not None:
        (p["project"] / "VISION.md").write_text(vision)
        (p["evidence"] / "vision.md").write_text(vision)
    if anti_patterns is not None:
        (p["project"] / "ANTI-PATTERNS.md").write_text(anti_patterns)
        (p["evidence"] / "anti-patterns.md").write_text(anti_patterns)
    (p["profile"] / ".claude.json").write_text(json.dumps({
        "hasCompletedOnboarding": True, "theme": "dark",
        "customApiKeyResponses": {"approved": [SYNTHETIC_KEY]},
    }))
    p["rules"].write_text("")
    cfg = {"run": str(run), "repo": str(repo), "claude": claude, "token": secrets.token_hex(16), "ttl": a.ttl,
           "columns": columns, "rows": rows, "started": time.time(),
           "no_vision": a.no_vision, "anti_patterns": anti_patterns is not None,
           "surface": a.surface}
    if desktop:
        cfg.update(cli=claude, cli_source=source, app_build=desk.is_app_build(claude),
                   max_rows=12 if a.max_rows is None else a.max_rows,
                   attach_later=a.attach_later, notifications_host=a.notifications_host)
    write_json(p["config"], cfg)
    try:
        with open(p["evidence"] / "server.log", "a") as log:
            subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), "_serve", str(run)],
                             stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=log,
                             start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
        deadline = time.monotonic() + 10
        while not read_json(p["server"]) and time.monotonic() < deadline:
            time.sleep(0.05)
        server = read_json(p["server"])
        if not server or not endpoint_is_ours(p, cfg):
            raise Failure("The scripted model endpoint did not start")
        cfg.update(server_pid=server["pid"], port=server["port"], server_verified=True,
                   server_identity=desk.proc_identity(server["pid"]))
        write_json(p["config"], cfg)
        if desktop:
            start_desktop(a, p, cfg)
            print(run)
            print(p["evidence"])
            return
        probe_unix_socket(p)
        made = tmux(p, "-f", "/dev/null", "new-session", "-d", "-x", str(columns), "-y",
                    str(rows), "-c", str(p["project"]), *isolated_env(p, server["port"]), claude,
                    "--plugin-dir", str(repo), "--setting-sources", "", "--strict-mcp-config",
                    "--tools", "")
        if made.returncode != 0 or "error creating" in made.stderr:
            if "Operation not permitted" in made.stderr:
                raise Failure(SOCKET_REFUSED)
            raise Failure("tmux could not start its server: " + made.stderr.strip())
        ids = tmux(p, "display-message", "-p", "#{pid} #{pane_pid}", check=True).stdout.split()
        cfg.update(tmux_pid=int(ids[0]), claude_pid=int(ids[1]),
                   tmux_identity=desk.proc_identity(int(ids[0])),
                   # The pane may still run env, which execs Claude: keep the start time only.
                   claude_identity=start_only(desk.proc_identity(int(ids[1]))))
        write_json(p["config"], cfg)
        project = str(p["project"])
        # A fresh profile always asks; accept only for this run's own fixture.
        wait_screen(p, "trust", lambda v: project in v and "❯ No, exit" in v
                    and "Yes, I trust this folder" in v, 30,
                    "the workspace trust prompt for the fixture")
        time.sleep(0.8)
        tmux(p, "send-keys", "Down", check=True)
        wait_screen(p, "trust", lambda v: "❯ Yes, I trust this folder" in v, 10,
                    "the trust choice to move to Yes")
        tmux(p, "send-keys", "Enter", check=True)
        view = wait_screen(p, "launch", is_ready, 30, "a usable prompt")
        (p["evidence"] / "launch.txt").write_text(view)
        log_action(p, "start", {"vision": a.vision, "no_vision": a.no_vision,
                                "anti_patterns": a.anti_patterns, "columns": columns,
                                "rows": rows,
                                "ttl": a.ttl, "port": cfg["port"], "server_pid": cfg["server_pid"],
                                "tmux_pid": cfg["tmux_pid"], "claude_pid": cfg["claude_pid"],
                                "socket": str(p["socket"])})
    except BaseException as error:
        try:
            stop(run)
        except Failure:
            pass
        raise Failure(f"start failed: {error}\nEvidence: {p['evidence']}") from None
    print(run)
    print(p["evidence"])


def start_desktop(a, p, cfg):
    """Starts the desktop host daemon, which spawns the CLI, sends initialize and (unless
    --attach-later) ui_attach, and records its port in scratch/host.json."""
    with open(p["evidence"] / "host.log", "a") as log:
        proc = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), "_host",
                                 str(p["run"])], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log,
                                stderr=log, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    cfg.update(host_pid=proc.pid, host_identity=desk.proc_identity(proc.pid))
    write_json(p["config"], cfg)
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 120

    def finished():
        """host.json once the host finished its start. The host writes it first right after
        it spawned the CLI (pid and identity, no "initialize"); stop reads the CLI pid there."""
        h = read_json(p["host"]) or {}
        if h.get("cli_pid") and cfg.get("cli_pid") != h["cli_pid"]:
            cfg.update(cli_pid=h["cli_pid"], cli_identity=h.get("cli_identity"))
            write_json(p["config"], cfg)
        return h if "initialize" in h else None

    while not finished() and time.monotonic() < deadline:
        if proc.poll() is not None:
            if finished():
                break  # it stopped its CLI after a failed initialize and recorded why
            raise Failure(f"The desktop host exited with {proc.returncode}; see "
                          f"{p['evidence'] / 'host.log'}")
        time.sleep(0.1)
    started = finished()
    if not started:
        raise Failure("The desktop host did not finish initialize within 120s")
    # The host is the CLI's parent and read its identity itself; this shell may not.
    cfg.update(cli_pid=started["cli_pid"], cli_identity=started.get("cli_identity"),
               host_port=started.get("port"))
    write_json(p["config"], cfg)
    if started.get("initialize") != "success":
        raise Failure(f"The CLI did not answer initialize: {started.get('error')}")
    health = host(p, cfg, "health")
    if not health.get("cli_alive"):
        raise Failure("The CLI exited after initialize; see evidence/cli-stderr.log")
    log_action(p, "start", {"surface": "desktop", "cli": cfg["cli"], "cli_source": cfg["cli_source"],
                            "app_build": cfg["app_build"], "version": health.get("version"),
                            "vision": a.vision, "no_vision": a.no_vision,
                            "anti_patterns": a.anti_patterns, "columns": cfg["columns"],
                            "max_rows": cfg["max_rows"], "attach_later": cfg["attach_later"],
                            "notifications_host": cfg["notifications_host"], "ttl": a.ttl,
                            "port": cfg["port"], "server_pid": cfg["server_pid"],
                            "host_pid": cfg["host_pid"], "host_port": cfg["host_port"],
                            "cli_pid": cfg["cli_pid"], "surfaces": health.get("surfaces")})


def version_tuple(text):
    match = re.search(r"(\d+)\.(\d+)\.(\d+)", text)
    return tuple(int(x) for x in match.groups()) if match else None


def status_line(p, cfg):
    """The status text that doctor expects from /course-keeper, and its description."""
    if cfg.get("no_vision"):
        return NO_VISION_STATUS, "the status line for a missing vision file"
    return ("VISION.md: " + str(p["project"] / "VISION.md"),
            "the status line with the fixture vision path")


def doctor_desktop(p, cfg, report):
    try:
        h = desk.call(p, cfg, "health")
    except desk.HostError as error:
        h = {"error": str(error)}
    host_ok = h.get("pid") == cfg["host_pid"] and pid_alive(cfg["host_pid"])
    cli_ok = (h.get("cli_pid") == cfg["cli_pid"] and h.get("cli_alive") is True
              and pid_alive(cfg["cli_pid"]))
    report("host", host_ok and cli_ok,
           f"host pid {h.get('pid', '-')} answers on 127.0.0.1:{cfg.get('host_port')} with this "
           f"run's token and runs CLI pid {h.get('cli_pid', '-')} "
           f"({'alive' if h.get('cli_alive') else 'not alive'}); start launched host "
           f"{cfg['host_pid']} and CLI {cfg['cli_pid']}" + (f"; {h['error']}" if "error" in h else ""))
    version = version_tuple(h.get("version") or "")
    build = ("the desktop app's pinned build" if desk.is_app_build(cfg["cli"])
             else "another binary, not the desktop app's pinned build")
    report("version", version is not None and version >= MIN_VERSION,
           f"{h.get('version')} (needs 2.1.323 or later), from the initialize response; "
           f"{build}: {cfg['cli']}")
    ours = endpoint_is_ours(p, cfg)
    report("endpoint", ours, f"127.0.0.1:{cfg['port']} "
           f"{'answered with this run token' if ours else 'did not answer with this run token'}")
    commands, caps = h.get("commands") or [], h.get("capabilities") or []
    report("initialize", "course-keeper" in commands and "ui_surface_v1" in caps,
           f"commands {'include' if 'course-keeper' in commands else 'lack'} course-keeper; "
           f"capabilities {'include' if 'ui_surface_v1' in caps else 'lack'} ui_surface_v1")
    if not h.get("attached"):
        report("surfaces", bool(cfg.get("attach_later")) and h.get("surfaces") is None,
               "not attached yet (started with --attach-later)" if cfg.get("attach_later")
               else "not attached, although start sends ui_attach")
    else:
        report("surfaces", h.get("surfaces") == ["desktop"],
               f"ui_attach answered surfaces {json.dumps(h.get('surfaces'))}")
    status, describe = status_line(p, cfg)
    if host_ok and cli_ok:
        try:
            send_desktop(p, cfg, "/course-keeper")
            view = wait_screen(p, "doctor", lambda v: contains(
                after(v, "❯ /course-keeper\n"), status), 20, describe,
                read=lambda: desktop_view(p, cfg))
            (p["evidence"] / "doctor.txt").write_text(view)
            report("plugin", True, f"/course-keeper shows {status}")
        except Failure as error:
            report("plugin", False, str(error).split("\n")[0])
    else:
        report("plugin", False, "not checked: the host or the CLI is not the one start launched")


def cmd_doctor(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    results = []

    def report(name, ok, detail):
        results.append(ok)
        print(f"{'ok  ' if ok else 'FAIL'} {name}: {detail}", flush=True)

    if is_desktop(cfg):
        doctor_desktop(p, cfg, report)
        if not all(results):
            sys.exit(1)
        return
    alive = tmux(p, "has-session").returncode == 0
    pane = tmux(p, "display-message", "-p", "#{pid} #{pane_pid} #{pane_dead}").stdout.split()
    same = (alive and len(pane) == 3 and int(pane[0]) == cfg["tmux_pid"]
            and int(pane[1]) == cfg["claude_pid"] and pane[2] == "0"
            and pid_command(cfg["claude_pid"]).startswith(cfg["claude"] + " "))
    report("tmux", same, f"server {pane[0] if pane else '-'} on {p['socket']}, pane runs pid "
           f"{pane[1] if len(pane) > 1 else '-'} (start launched server {cfg['tmux_pid']}, "
           f"Claude {cfg['claude_pid']})")
    run = subprocess.run([*isolated_env(p, cfg["port"]), cfg["claude"], "--version"],
                         text=True, capture_output=True, timeout=30)
    version = version_tuple(run.stdout)
    report("version", version is not None and version >= MIN_VERSION,
           f"{run.stdout.strip() or run.stderr.strip()} (needs 2.1.323 or later)")
    ours = endpoint_is_ours(p, cfg)
    report("endpoint", ours, f"127.0.0.1:{cfg['port']} "
           f"{'answered with this run token' if ours else 'did not answer with this run token'}")
    if cfg.get("no_vision"):
        status = NO_VISION_STATUS
        describe = "the status line for a missing vision file"
    else:
        status = "VISION.md: " + str(p["project"] / "VISION.md")
        describe = "the status line with the fixture vision path"
    if same:
        try:
            send_text(p, "/course-keeper")
            view = wait_screen(p, "doctor", lambda v: contains(
                after(v, "❯ /course-keeper\n"), status), 20, describe)
            (p["evidence"] / "doctor.txt").write_text(view)
            report("plugin", True, f"/course-keeper shows {status}")
        except Failure as error:
            report("plugin", False, str(error).split("\n")[0])
    else:
        report("plugin", False, "not checked: the session is not the one start launched")
    if not all(results):
        sys.exit(1)


def send_text(p, text):
    """Types text, presses Enter and returns once the input line is empty again.

    The prompt takes the text at that moment and its echo is the newest one on
    the screen, so a later wait --after the echo never reads an older answer.
    """
    tmux(p, "send-keys", "-l", text, check=True)
    time.sleep(0.3)
    tmux(p, "send-keys", "Enter", check=True)
    log_action(p, "send", {"text": text})
    wait_screen(p, "send", lambda v: input_line(v) == "❯", 15,
                "the prompt to take the text (an empty input line)", history=False)


def send_desktop(p, cfg, text, bare=False, reminder=None):
    """Writes one user frame as the app does and returns once the CLI took it."""
    took = host(p, cfg, "send", {"text": text, "bare": bare, "reminder": reminder},
                timeout=desk.TAKE_TIMEOUT + 15)
    log_action(p, "send", {"text": text, "bare": bare, "reminder": reminder,
                           "uuid": took.get("uuid"), "deferred": took.get("deferred")})
    if "error" in took:
        raise Failure(f"send failed: {took['error']}")
    if not took.get("taken"):
        if took.get("written") is False:
            raise Failure(f"not sent: the turn before it did not end within {desk.TAKE_TIMEOUT}s; "
                          f"the host dropped the held frame {took.get('uuid')}, so a retry "
                          "sends the prompt once")
        raise Failure(f"sent, not acknowledged: the CLI did not take the frame within "
                      f"{desk.TAKE_TIMEOUT}s: no command_lifecycle or status frame named its "
                      f"uuid {took.get('uuid')}")


def cmd_send(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    if is_desktop(cfg):
        return send_desktop(p, cfg, a.text, a.bare, a.reminder)
    if a.bare or a.reminder is not None:
        raise Failure("--bare and --reminder apply to a desktop run only (they shape its user frame).")
    send_text(p, a.text)


KEYBOARD_ONLY = ("{name} drives the terminal's keyboard, which a desktop run does not have; use "
                 "`control press RUN <label part | dismiss>`, which sends ui_press as the app does for "
                 "a click.")


def cmd_keys(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    terminal_only(cfg, KEYBOARD_ONLY.format(name="keys"))
    for i, key in enumerate(a.key):
        if i:
            time.sleep(0.15)
        tmux(p, "send-keys", key, check=True)
    log_action(p, "keys", {"keys": a.key})


def cmd_focus(a):
    """Gives the alert row the keyboard and prints the label of the button that holds it."""
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    terminal_only(cfg, KEYBOARD_ONLY.format(name="focus"))
    print(focus_row(p))


def focus_row(p):
    """Sends ctrl+x and Tab and returns the label of the row button that takes the focus."""
    tmux(p, "send-keys", "C-x", check=True)
    time.sleep(0.15)
    tmux(p, "send-keys", "Tab", check=True)
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 5
    while True:
        label = focused_button(capture(p, history=False, ansi=True))
        if label:
            log_action(p, "focus", {"button": label})
            return label
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            view = capture(p, history=False)
            (p["evidence"] / "focus-timeout.txt").write_text(view)
            log_action(p, "focus", {"button": None})
            raise Failure("No row button took the focus within 5s (none is drawn in inverse "
                          f"video). Last screen: {p['evidence'] / 'focus-timeout.txt'}\n{tail(view)}")
        time.sleep(0.2)


def cmd_press(a):
    """Presses a row button by hotkey or label part and prints its label."""
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    if is_desktop(cfg):
        out = host(p, cfg, "press", {"which": a.which}, timeout=90)
        log_action(p, "press", {"which": a.which, **{k: out.get(k) for k in
                                                       ("label", "hotkey", "sent", "answer", "error")}})
        if "error" in out:
            raise Failure(out["error"])
        answer = out.get("answer") or {}
        if answer.get("subtype") != "success" or (answer.get("response") or {}).get("handled") \
                is not True:
            raise Failure(f"The CLI did not handle the press of {out.get('label')!r}: "
                          f"{json.dumps(answer)[:400]}")
        print(out["label"])
        return

    def listing(buttons):
        return [f"{k}: {v}" for k, v in buttons.items()] or \
            "none (no alert row is on the visible pane)"

    def refuse(message):
        log_action(p, "press", {"which": a.which, "key": None, "refused": message})
        raise Failure(message)

    # Resolve the button from the visible pane before any key goes in: a refusal sends nothing.
    buttons = row_buttons(capture(p, history=False))
    w = a.which.strip().lower()
    if a.which in buttons:
        keys = [a.which]
    else:
        keys = [k for k, label in buttons.items() if label.lower() == w] or \
               [k for k, label in buttons.items() if w in label.lower()]
    if not keys:
        refuse(f"No button {a.which!r} is drawn. The row's buttons: {listing(buttons)}.")
    if len(keys) > 1:
        refuse(f"{a.which!r} names {len(keys)} buttons: {[f'{k}: {buttons[k]}' for k in keys]}. "
               "Give more of the label.")
    key, label = keys[0], buttons[keys[0]]
    focus_row(p)
    now = row_buttons(capture(p, history=False))
    if now.get(key) != label:
        refuse(f"The row changed while it took the focus: hotkey {key} was {label!r} and is now "
               f"{now.get(key)!r}; no hotkey was sent. The row's buttons: {listing(now)}.")
    tmux(p, "send-keys", key, check=True)
    log_action(p, "press", {"which": a.which, "key": key, "label": label})
    print(label)


def cmd_attach(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    desktop_only(cfg, "attach")
    answer = host(p, cfg, "attach", timeout=90)
    log_action(p, "attach", answer)
    if answer.get("subtype") != "success":
        raise Failure(f"ui_attach failed: {json.dumps(answer)[:400]}")
    print("surfaces: " + json.dumps((answer.get("response") or {}).get("surfaces")))


def cmd_messages(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    desktop_only(cfg, "messages")
    frames = host(p, cfg, "messages")["system"]
    text = "".join(json.dumps(f) + "\n" for f in frames
                   if a.type is None or f.get("subtype") == a.type)
    if a.save:
        (p["evidence"] / (a.save + ".txt")).write_text(text)
    sys.stdout.write(text)


def cmd_screen(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    if is_desktop(cfg):
        if a.tree:
            view = json.dumps(host(p, cfg, "screen")["tree"], indent=1) + "\n"
        else:
            view = desktop_view(p, cfg, row=a.visible)
    else:
        view = capture(p, history=not a.visible, ansi=a.ansi)
    if a.save:
        (p["evidence"] / (a.save + ".txt")).write_text(saved_view(p, cfg, view, a.visible))
    sys.stdout.write(view)


def cmd_wait(a):
    p, cfg = config(a.run)
    label = a.save or "wait"

    def matches(view):
        if a.after is not None and a.after not in view:
            return False  # --after requires the mark, with or without --gone
        found = contains(after(view, a.after), a.text)
        return not found if a.gone else found

    what = ("the screen to lose " if a.gone else "the screen to show ") + repr(a.text)
    read = (lambda: desktop_view(p, cfg, row=a.visible)) if is_desktop(cfg) else None
    try:
        view = wait_screen(p, label, matches, a.timeout, what, history=not a.visible, read=read)
    except Failure as error:
        last = p["evidence"] / (label + "-timeout.txt")
        if a.after is not None and a.after not in (last.read_text() if last.exists() else ""):
            raise Failure(f"Timed out after {a.timeout}s: the mark {a.after!r} was not found on "
                          f"the screen, so {what} was not checked. Last screen: {last}") from None
        raise error
    if a.save:
        (p["evidence"] / (a.save + ".txt")).write_text(saved_view(p, cfg, view, a.visible))


def cmd_reply(a):
    p, _ = config(a.run)
    text = Path(a.file).read_text() if a.file else a.text
    if a.delay is not None and a.delay < 0:
        raise Failure("--delay takes a number of seconds of 0 or more")
    if a.times is not None and a.times < 1:
        raise Failure("--times takes a count of 1 or more")
    rule = {"when": a.when, "text": text, "model": a.model, "times": a.times,
            "unless": a.unless or [], "delay": a.delay}
    with open(p["rules"], "a") as f:
        f.write(json.dumps(rule) + "\n")
    index = len([x for x in p["rules"].read_text().splitlines() if x.strip()]) - 1
    log_action(p, "reply", {**rule, "index": index})
    print(f"rule {index}")


def read_requests(p):
    """The request log's rows, and the numbers of the lines that are not valid JSON (a line
    that the endpoint was still writing when it exited). Raises OSError without a log."""
    rows, skipped = [], []
    lines = (p["evidence"] / "model-requests.jsonl").read_text().splitlines()
    for number, line in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        try:
            row = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            skipped.append(number)
            continue
        if isinstance(row, dict):
            rows.append(row)
        else:
            skipped.append(number)
    return rows, skipped


UNSCRIPTED = ("default", "unknown path")


def requests_text(p, unscripted=False):
    """The request listing that `control requests` prints, and how many rows it holds that
    no rule answered (matched "default" or "unknown path"). With unscripted, only those rows
    are listed. A last line names the log lines that were skipped as not valid JSON."""
    rows = []
    unanswered = 0
    found, skipped = read_requests(p)
    for r in found:
        if r.get("matched") in UNSCRIPTED:
            unanswered += 1
        elif unscripted:
            continue
        first = " ".join((r.get("last_user") or "").split())[:120]
        rows.append(f"{r.get('seq')}\t{r.get('method')} {r.get('path')}\t{r.get('model')}\t"
                    f"stream={'yes' if r.get('stream') else 'no'}\t{r.get('matched')}\t{first}")
    if skipped:
        rows.append(f"skipped {len(skipped)} line{'s' if len(skipped) > 1 else ''} of "
                    f"model-requests.jsonl that {'are' if len(skipped) > 1 else 'is'} not valid "
                    f"JSON: line {', '.join(map(str, skipped))}")
    return "\n".join(rows) + ("\n" if rows else ""), unanswered


def cmd_requests(a):
    p = paths(a.run)
    if run_state(p) is None:
        raise not_a_run(p)
    log = p["evidence"] / "model-requests.jsonl"
    try:
        text, unanswered = requests_text(p, a.unscripted)
    except OSError as error:
        raise Failure(f"Cannot read the request log {log}: {error.strerror or error}") from None
    if a.save:
        (p["evidence"] / (a.save + ".txt")).write_text(text)
    sys.stdout.write(text)
    if a.unscripted and unanswered:
        sys.exit(1)


def cmd_store(a):
    p, _ = config(a.run)
    entries = []
    for path in sorted((p["profile"] / "plugins" / "store").glob("course-keeper*.json")):
        data = read_json(path, {})
        for key, value in data.items():
            if isinstance(value, dict):
                entries.append({"file": path.name, "key": key, **value})
    entries.sort(key=lambda e: e.get("savedAt") or 0)
    text = json.dumps(entries[-1] if entries else None, indent=2) + "\n"
    if a.save:
        (p["evidence"] / (a.save + ".json")).write_text(text)
    sys.stdout.write(text)


def recorded_pids(p, cfg):
    """(name, pid, identity) of every process that start recorded for the run."""
    if is_desktop(cfg):
        host_json = read_json(p["host"]) or {}
        out = [("cli", cfg.get("cli_pid") or host_json.get("cli_pid"),
                cfg.get("cli_identity") or host_json.get("cli_identity")),
               ("host process", cfg.get("host_pid"), cfg.get("host_identity"))]
    else:
        out = [("claude", cfg.get("claude_pid"), cfg.get("claude_identity")),
               ("tmux", cfg.get("tmux_pid"), cfg.get("tmux_identity"))]
    return out + [("endpoint", cfg.get("server_pid"), cfg.get("server_identity"))]


def end_pid(name, pid, identity, seconds, done):
    """Waits for a recorded pid; one that outlives the wait gets SIGTERM by the rule of
    signal_recorded. Adds what happened to done[name]."""
    before = done[name] + ", then " if name in done else ""
    if pid is None:
        done[name] = before + "never started"
        return
    if wait_gone(pid, seconds):
        done[name] = before + f"pid {pid} exited"
        return
    sent = signal_recorded(pid, identity)
    done[name] = before + sent
    if not sent.startswith("not signalled") and " refused" not in sent:
        done[name] += ", exited" if wait_gone(pid, 5) else ", STILL RUNNING"


def teardown(p, cfg, note=None, endpoint_is_self=False):
    """The one teardown of a live run, for stop and for the TTL: saves the final screen and
    the request listing, stops the run's processes, writes the stop record and returns the
    processes of the run that still run (a list of texts; empty when teardown is complete).
    It does not touch scratch/. endpoint_is_self: the caller is the endpoint, which exits
    after this; it is not stopped or counted."""
    done = {} if note is None else {"note": note}
    desktop = is_desktop(cfg)
    # Evidence first: the screen is gone once tmux closes or the host exits.
    try:
        (p["evidence"] / "final-screen.txt").write_text(
            desktop_view(p, cfg) if desktop else capture(p))
        done["final screen"] = "saved"
    except Exception as error:
        done["final screen"] = "not saved: " + str(error).split("\n")[0]
    try:
        (p["evidence"] / "model-requests.txt").write_text(requests_text(p)[0])
        done["requests"] = "saved"
    except Exception as error:  # the log never stops a stop
        done["requests"] = "not saved: " + str(error).split("\n")[0]
    if desktop:
        stop_desktop(p, cfg, done)
    else:
        if p["socket"].exists():
            done["tmux"] = "kill-server: " + ("ok" if tmux(p, "kill-server").returncode == 0
                                              else "no server")
        end_pid("claude", cfg.get("claude_pid"), cfg.get("claude_identity"), 10, done)
        end_pid("tmux", cfg.get("tmux_pid"), cfg.get("tmux_identity"), 5, done)
    if endpoint_is_self:
        done["endpoint"] = "runs this teardown and exits after it"
    else:
        pid = cfg.get("server_pid")
        done["endpoint"] = "not running"
        if pid_alive(pid):
            try:
                endpoint(p, cfg, CONTROL_PREFIX + "shutdown", "POST")
                done["endpoint"] = "shutdown request"
            except (OSError, ValueError, urllib.error.URLError, Failure):
                done["endpoint"] = "shutdown request failed"
            end_pid("endpoint", pid, cfg.get("server_identity"), 5, done)
    alive = [f"{name} pid {pid}" for name, pid, identity in recorded_pids(p, cfg)
             if pid and not (endpoint_is_self and name == "endpoint")
             and recorded_alive(pid, identity)]
    if alive:
        done["still running"] = alive
        done["scratch"] = "kept, so that a later stop can retry"
    log_action(p, "stop", done)
    return alive


def stop(run):
    """Tears a live run down and removes scratch/. Refuses a directory that is not a run.
    Raises Failure, and keeps scratch/, when a process of the run still runs."""
    p = paths(run)
    state = run_state(p)
    if state is None:
        raise not_a_run(p)
    if state == "live":
        alive = teardown(p, read_json(p["config"]))
        if alive:
            raise Failure(f"stop is incomplete: still running: {'; '.join(alive)}. scratch/ "
                          f"stays, so that a later stop can retry. Stop record: "
                          f"{p['evidence'] / 'actions.log'}")
        shutil.rmtree(p["scratch"], ignore_errors=True)
    return p["evidence"]


def stop_desktop(p, cfg, done):
    """Asks the host to stop (it closes the CLI's stdin first and signals only the CLI's own
    process group), then waits for the recorded pids. A recorded pid that outlives that gets
    SIGTERM only when it still shows the start time that start recorded for it (see
    signal_recorded); nothing else is signalled. The CLI pid comes from scratch/run.json, or
    from scratch/host.json when start did not get to copy it."""
    cli_exit = None
    try:
        cli_exit = desk.call(p, cfg, "health", timeout=5).get("cli_exit")
    except desk.HostError:
        pass
    try:
        desk.call(p, cfg, "stop", timeout=5)
        done["host"] = "stop request (the host closes the CLI's stdin first)"
    except desk.HostError as error:
        done["host"] = "no answer to the stop request: " + str(error)
    for (name, pid, identity), seconds in zip(recorded_pids(p, cfg)[:2], (20, 10)):
        end_pid(name, pid, identity, seconds, done)
        if name == "cli" and cli_exit is not None and done[name].endswith("exited"):
            done[name] += f" (it had exited with code {cli_exit} before stop)"


def cmd_stop(a):
    print(stop(a.run))


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="control", description=__doc__,
                                     formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    s = sub.add_parser("start")
    group = s.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    group.add_argument("--vision")
    group.add_argument("--no-vision", action="store_true",
                       help="the fixture project gets no VISION.md")
    s.add_argument("--anti-patterns", metavar="FILE",
                   help="also write FILE as ANTI-PATTERNS.md beside VISION.md")
    s.add_argument("--surface", choices=("terminal", "desktop"), default="terminal")
    s.add_argument("--columns", type=int,
                   help="terminal: pane width (150); desktop: the bodyColumns prop (96)")
    s.add_argument("--rows", type=int, help="terminal only: pane height (42)")
    s.add_argument("--cli", metavar="PATH",
                   help="desktop only: the CLI to run (default: the desktop app's newest "
                        "verified build, or $CLAUDE_DESKTOP_BIN)")
    s.add_argument("--attach-later", action="store_true",
                   help="desktop only: send no ui_attach until `control attach`")
    s.add_argument("--notifications-host", action="store_true",
                   help="desktop only: set CLAUDE_CODE_NOTIFICATIONS_HOST=1")
    s.add_argument("--max-rows", type=int, help="desktop only: the maxRows prop (12)")
    s.add_argument("--ttl", type=float, default=30)
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_start)
    for name, fn in (("doctor", cmd_doctor), ("stop", cmd_stop), ("focus", cmd_focus),
                     ("attach", cmd_attach)):
        s = sub.add_parser(name)
        s.add_argument("run")
        s.set_defaults(fn=fn)
    s = sub.add_parser("send")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("text")
    s.add_argument("--bare", action="store_true",
                   help="desktop only: a frame without client_platform (not a person's)")
    s.add_argument("--reminder", metavar="TEXT",
                   help="desktop only: send the content as an array whose first block is a "
                        "<system-reminder> block with TEXT")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_send)
    s = sub.add_parser("press")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("which", metavar="LABEL-PART|dismiss|HOTKEY")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_press)
    s = sub.add_parser("keys")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("key", nargs="+")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_keys)
    s = sub.add_parser("messages")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("--type", metavar="SUBTYPE", help="only system frames of this subtype")
    s.add_argument("--save")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_messages)
    for name, fn in (("screen", cmd_screen), ("requests", cmd_requests), ("store", cmd_store)):
        s = sub.add_parser(name)
        s.add_argument("run")
        s.add_argument("--save")
        if name == "requests":
            s.add_argument("--unscripted", action="store_true",
                           help="only the requests that matched no rule; exit 1 if there is one")
        if name == "screen":
            s.add_argument("--visible", "--row", dest="visible", action="store_true",
                           help="terminal: only the visible pane; desktop: only the row")
            s.add_argument("--ansi", action="store_true",
                           help="terminal only: keep colors and attributes")
            s.add_argument("--tree", action="store_true",
                           help="desktop only: the latest AbovePrompt tree as JSON")
        s.set_defaults(fn=fn)
    s = sub.add_parser("wait")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("text")
    s.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=30)
    s.add_argument("--gone", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--after", help="match only the screen after the last occurrence of this text")
    s.add_argument("--visible", "--row", dest="visible", action="store_true",
                   help="terminal: match only the visible pane; desktop: only the row")
    s.add_argument("--save")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_wait)
    s = sub.add_parser("reply")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.add_argument("--when", required=True)
    group = s.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    group.add_argument("--text")
    group.add_argument("--file")
    s.add_argument("--model")
    s.add_argument("--times", type=int)
    s.add_argument("--unless", action="append", metavar="SUBSTRING",
                   help="no match when the last user message holds SUBSTRING (repeatable)")
    s.add_argument("--delay", type=float, metavar="SECONDS",
                   help="hold a matched request this long before the answer")
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_reply)
    s = sub.add_parser("_serve")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: serve(a.run))
    s = sub.add_parser("_host")
    s.add_argument("run")
    s.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: desk.daemon(paths(a.run), read_json(paths(a.run)["config"]),
                                            SYNTHETIC_KEY))
    a = parser.parse_args()
    try:
        a.fn(a)
    except Failure as error:
        print(str(error), file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(1)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
